<div class="infographic rounded-lg overflow-hidden" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;"><div class="rounded-xl overflow-hidden" style="background-color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;"><div class="p-6 pb-4"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4"><div class="flex-1"><h1 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2" style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255); font-weight: 700;">Regional Infrastructure Cluster (RIC) Regeneration Platform</h1><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); line-height: 1.75;">A cloud-based workflow engine bridging citizen reporting with professional engineering execution to automate infrastructure maintenance for labor-constrained municipalities.</p></div><div class="px-4 py-2 rounded-lg text-center flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(236, 253, 245);"><span class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1" style="color: rgb(16, 185, 129);">Decision</span><span class="text-lg font-bold block" style="color: rgb(16, 185, 129);">Proceed</span></div></div></div><div class="px-6 py-4 flex items-center gap-6" style="background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2"><svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17.657 16.657L13.414 20.9a1.998 1.998 0 01-2.827 0l-4.244-4.243a8 8 0 1111.314 0z"></path><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 11a3 3 0 11-6 0 3 3 0 016 0z"></path></svg><span class="text-sm" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);">Japan (Regional Municipalities)</span></div><div class="w-px h-4" style="background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);"></div><p class="text-sm flex-1" style="color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);">Aligns with mandate to solve infrastructure crisis and transition to recurring revenue, contingent on bridging digital capability gaps and validating municipal procurement.</p></div></div><div class="p-6" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-5 pb-4" style="border-bottom: 2px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;"><span class="text-lg font-bold" style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">1</span></div><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;">Overview</h2><p class="text-sm mt-0.5" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Project description, recommendation, and key risks</p></div></div><div class="space-y-5"><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5" style=""><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider block mb-3" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Project Description</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">The proposal involves building a software platform business to automate defect identification and repair for aging infrastructure, leveraging engineering expertise. The business model depends on establishing a subscription-based revenue stream with municipalities accustomed to project-based contracts.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="mb-4"><span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider block mb-2" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Decision Statement</span><span class="text-xl font-bold" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Conditional Fit</span></div><div><span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider block mb-2" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Recommendation</span><p class="text-sm" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105);">Success is contingent on the organization's ability to bridge the digital capability gap and validate that municipalities can legally procure subscription software outside of traditional construction budgets.</p></div></div></div><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(236, 253, 245); border: 2px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.19);"><div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4"><div class="flex-1"><span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider block mb-2" style="color: rgb(16, 185, 129);">Path Forward</span><p class="text-base font-semibold mb-2">Proceed with Caution (Yellow Light) to fund a specific 12-month pilot rather than full scaling.</p><p class="text-sm" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105);">Execute a 'Partnership-Led Narrow Platform' strategy focusing on digitizing Steps 2–3 (Inspection/Design) via a 'Cluster' sales motion, while partnering for Step 1 (Citizen Reporting) and utilizing an internal product ownership model.</p></div><span class="px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: rgb(16, 185, 129); border: 1px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.19);">High Confidence</span></div></div><div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3"><div class="w-1.5 h-5 rounded-full" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68);"></div><span class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85);">Key Risks (13)</span></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-3"><div class="rounded-lg p-4" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(254, 242, 242); color: rgb(239, 68, 68);">HIGH</span><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Procurement Structural Barriers</span><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Municipal budget structures (Capex vs. Opex) and local-only bidding rules legally prevent centralized SaaS adoption, potentially rendering the serviceable market size near zero.</p></div></div></div><div class="rounded-lg p-4" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(254, 242, 242); color: rgb(239, 68, 68);">HIGH</span><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Unit Economic Viability</span><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">The business model is financially unviable at the single-municipality level due to high CAC and low price points, requiring an unproven 'Cluster' sales motion to succeed.</p></div></div></div><div class="rounded-lg p-4" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(254, 242, 242); color: rgb(239, 68, 68);">HIGH</span><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Execution and Culture Gap</span><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">The team's deep engineering authority combined with a lack of SaaS DNA creates a risk that the 'Zero-Defect' manufacturing culture will stifle necessary agile software iteration.</p></div></div></div><div class="rounded-lg p-4" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(254, 242, 242); color: rgb(239, 68, 68);">HIGH</span><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Liability Exposure</span><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Acting as a platform orchestrator could expose the parent company to uninsurable liability for infrastructure failures if the legal distinction between information provision and engineering judgment is not strictly defined.</p></div></div></div><div class="rounded-lg p-4" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(254, 242, 242); color: rgb(239, 68, 68);">HIGH</span><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Service Margin Trap</span><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Failure to successfully automate the inspection diagnosis workflow could permanently anchor gross margins at consulting levels (30-40%) rather than the targeted SaaS levels (70%+).</p></div></div></div><div class="rounded-lg p-4" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded text-xs font-bold flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(254, 242, 242); color: rgb(239, 68, 68);">HIGH</span><div class="flex-1 min-w-0"><span class="font-semibold text-sm block mb-1">Cash Flow Trough</span><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Extended government sales cycles averaging 22 months create a projected ¥450M cash flow trough, requiring significant working capital funding before revenue compounds.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div style="background-color: rgb(241, 245, 249); height: 8px;"></div><div class="p-6" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-5 pb-4" style="border-bottom: 2px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;"><span class="text-lg font-bold" style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">2</span></div><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;">Strategic Fit Assessment</h2><p class="text-sm mt-0.5" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Can we do it? Should we do it?</p></div></div><div class="space-y-5"><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider block mb-3" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Assessment Summary</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">This opportunity represents a Conditional Fit. It aligns strongly with the organization's strategic mandate to solve the national infrastructure crisis and transition from labor-intensive services to high-margin recurring revenue. However, a significant tension exists between this high strategic attractiveness and the organization's current lack of internal software development capabilities and agile execution culture. Success is contingent on the organization's ability to bridge this digital capability gap and validate that municipalities can legally procure subscription software outside of traditional construction budgets.</p></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4" style=""><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 2px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.19);"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center" style="background-color: rgb(255, 251, 235);"><svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color: rgb(245, 158, 11);"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"></path></svg></div><span class="text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wide" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Can We Do It?</span></div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">Borderline (Low confidence). While NLM has the financial capital and engineering data, it currently lacks the software leadership and agile culture necessary to build a scalable platform without falling into a low-margin consulting trap. The organization possesses balance sheet strength to fund the projected ¥450M working capital trough and owns requisite historical data and engineering protocols. However, it faces friction from local-only bidding rules, and the sales force is optimized for construction bidding rather than software subscriptions. There is a Capability-Strategy Mismatch regarding digital execution, lacking a digital leader and internal software product management DNA, while the manufacturing-centric culture conflicts with iterative software development.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 2px solid rgba(16, 185, 129, 0.19);"><div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4"><div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center" style="background-color: rgb(236, 253, 245);"><svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24" style="color: rgb(16, 185, 129);"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"></path></svg></div><span class="text-base font-bold uppercase tracking-wide" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Should We Do It?</span></div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">Yes (High confidence). The venture targets an irreversible labor shortage with a proprietary engineering solution that software-only competitors cannot legally or technically replicate. The opportunity addresses a structural crisis where 25% of municipalities lack technical staff, with cumulative maintenance costs projected to reach ¥12.3 trillion by 2048. It aligns with the goal of transforming from a fee-for-service to a platform model, though the shift from CAPEX to OPEX presents friction. Nippon Light Metal possesses a defensible moat in the Resolution Gap (Steps 2–3) where pure software competitors lack the engineering authority to operate.</p></div></div></div></div><div style="height: 8px; background-color: rgb(241, 245, 249);"></div><div class="p-6" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-5 pb-4" style="border-bottom: 2px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;"><span class="text-lg font-bold" style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">3</span></div><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;">Gap Analysis &amp; Assumptions</h2><p class="text-sm mt-0.5" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Execution gaps and critical assumptions to validate</p></div></div><div class="space-y-6"><div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4"><div class="w-1.5 h-5 rounded-full" style="background-color: rgb(245, 158, 11);"></div><span class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85);">7T Framework Analysis</span></div><div class="grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-3"><div class="rounded-xl p-4" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2"><span class="text-xl">👥</span><span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Team</span></div><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">The venture lacks a CTO and internal software DNA, relying on external partners. This creates a 'Capability-Strategy Mismatch' for a digital platform play.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-4" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2"><span class="text-xl">📊</span><span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">TAM</span></div><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">The total addressable market is massive (¥12.3T deficit), driven by irreversible demographic trends. The sheer volume of aging assets guarantees demand.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-4" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2"><span class="text-xl">⚙️</span><span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Technology</span></div><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">The engineering logic exists within NLM, but the software platform is unbuilt. Integration with third-party data (FixMyStreet) poses technical uncertainty.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-4" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2"><span class="text-xl">📈</span><span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Traction</span></div><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">Currently at Pre-Seed/Validation phase. No paid pilots or recurring revenue have been secured yet to validate the business model.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-4" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2"><span class="text-xl">📋</span><span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Terms</span></div><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">The 22-month government sales cycle and rigid procurement rules (Capex vs Opex) create a severe liquidity risk and high barrier to entry.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-4" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2"><span class="text-xl">🔮</span><span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Trends</span></div><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">Strong tailwinds from labor shortages and MLIT mandates favor automation. The shift to 'preventive maintenance' aligns perfectly with the value proposition.</p></div><div class="rounded-xl p-4" style="background-color: rgb(248, 250, 252); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-2"><span class="text-xl">💰</span><span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Transactions</span></div><p class="text-xs leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">Revenue model unproven. No established unit economics, pricing validation, or payment cycles tested with actual government customers.</p></div></div></div><div><div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4"><div class="w-1.5 h-5 rounded-full" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68);"></div><span class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85);">Critical Assumptions (6)</span></div><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(254, 242, 242); border: 1px solid rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.125);"><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-3"><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">1</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">Municipalities can legally procure subscription-based software (Opex) using existing maintenance or DX budget codes without requiring multi-year legislative changes.</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">2</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">The 'Cluster Management' sales model successfully aggregates demand from multiple small municipalities to bypass local-only bidding restrictions.</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">3</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">Platform liability for missed defects ('false negatives') can be contractually separated from professional engineering liability to prevent uninsurable risk exposure.</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">4</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">Regional engineering consultants will adopt the platform as a productivity tool rather than blocking it as a threat to billable hours.</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">5</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">Citizen reporting data from third-party tools like FixMyStreet meets the technical granularity required for professional engineering diagnosis.</p></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><span class="w-6 h-6 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-xs font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(239, 68, 68); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">6</span><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed" style="color: rgb(51, 65, 85); line-height: 1.75;">The internal product team can effectively manage a software roadmap without a full-time internal CTO by using external technical partners.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div><div style="height: 8px; background-color: rgb(241, 245, 249);"></div><div class="p-6" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);"><div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-5 pb-4" style="border-bottom: 2px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0" style="background-color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;"><span class="text-lg font-bold" style="color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">4</span></div><div><h2 class="text-xl font-bold" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42); font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, &quot;Segoe UI&quot;, Roboto, sans-serif;">Key Highlights</h2><p class="text-sm mt-0.5" style="color: rgb(100, 116, 139);">Critical insights from exploration and testing</p></div></div><div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4"><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3 mb-3"><span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(15, 23, 42); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">1</span><h3 class="text-sm font-bold leading-tight pt-1" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Procurement Rules Legally Block SaaS Subscriptions</h3></div><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed mb-3" style="color: rgb(71, 85, 105); line-height: 1.75;">Municipal budgets rigidly separate Capex (construction) from Opex (software), often legally preventing subscription payments for infrastructure tools. The pilot must validate a specific 'Cluster' procurement loophole or budget code, or the serviceable market is effectively zero.</p><span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full text-xs font-medium" style="background-color: rgb(241, 245, 249); color: rgb(100, 116, 139);"><svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M7 7h.01M7 3h5c.512 0 1.024.195 1.414.586l7 7a2 2 0 010 2.828l-7 7a2 2 0 01-2.828 0l-7-7A1.994 1.994 0 013 12V7a4 4 0 014-4z"></path></svg>six-t-analysis</span></div><div class="rounded-xl p-5" style="background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); border: 1px solid rgb(226, 232, 240);"><div class="flex items-start gap-3 mb-3"><span class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm font-bold" style="background-color: rgb(15, 23, 42); color: rgb(255, 255, 255);">2</span><h3 class="text-sm font-bold leading-tight pt-1" style="color: rgb(15, 23, 42);">Unit Econom